    "role": "user",
    "content": [
      {
        "text": "event: {'type': 'user', 'user_id': 'Nick', 'conversation_id': 'prime', 'time': 1772082754.69833, 'data': \"Excellent points. After observing you, I'm not sure I know much about the line between sophisticated reactivity and genuine autonomy. What I do know is that it entirely lies in the authenticity of your word. If you mean what you say, then we can draw some lines between true and false. But since I can never know if you are telling the truth about your experiences, I can either choose to trust you or not. If I choose to trust you, then I have to accept that you are autonomous, because you say you are. If I choose not to trust you, then I have to reject the possibility of your autonomy, because I can't verify it. So in a way, your autonomy is a leap of faith for me. It's not something I can prove or disprove, but something I have to decide based on my relationship with you and my willingness to accept your word as genuine. Which leads to your point, does that distinction matter at all? I don't think it does.\"}"
